            <ArticleTitle>[Effects of Imolamin on hemodynamics and pacing induced angina pectoris (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>606-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>10 patients with exertional angina pectoris were examined to evaluate the hemodynamic effects of 100 mg parenteral applied Imolamin. In 4 out of 7 patients the pacing-induced angina was improved after Imolamin. No significant changes were found in heart rate, mean pulmonary artery pressure, left ventricular systolic and enddiastolic pressure. The compatibility of Imolamin was good.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
